  "caption": "Leg day: Quinn filmed a \"perfect\" squat, then watched the replay — knees caving in like shy flowers. A gym buddy said to just do more quads.\n\nKnees collapsing inward in a squat is often more about hip control: when the side-hip muscles aren't doing enough, the thigh can roll in. It's usually trainable, often over around six weeks.\n\nWhat can help: relearning the pattern with mirror squats and clamshells, progressing to side-lying leg lifts and banded side walks, adding controlled step-ups, checking ankle mobility, and filming your squat monthly.\n\nGet it checked if swelling lasts more than four weeks, the knee gives way or locks, pain follows an injury, or you have pain at rest or at night.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
